  "app_message": "T-2383: the Sauganash's two ridge stacks move out to the gable ends\n\nAndreas/Braunhold's 1884 plate draws both main-block stacks close to the ends of\nthe ridge \u2014 the near one immediately behind the visible gable peak. The record\ncarried the generic chimney_placement default (0.22/0.78 of the frontage), which\non the retained 9.92 m block put them about 1.6 m further inboard on each side.\nform.chimney_placement now selects the existing `gable_ends` kit: centres 0.60 m\nand 9.32 m. Confidence `reconstructed`.\n\nNo producer, archetype or kit code changed \u2014 this selects geometry the generator\nalready had. Exactly one asset went stale and exactly one was rebuilt, on the\npinned Blender 4.5.3 (Ubuntu 26.04), with its web derivative bound in the same\nrun: sauganash_hotel__frame_1831.glb. 1035 of 1035 assets match their inputs.\n\nThe 0.60 m inset, the 0.90 m square shaft and the ridge + 0.55 m top are the\nkit's reconstructed choices; the engraving supports the relative disposition and\nsupplies no coordinate, metre, July 1835 fitting date or historical camera.\ndocs/LIBERTIES.md L-sauganash-ridge-end-stacks-2383 records that.\n\nAll four Hotel-dependent controlled views were re-rendered from their own\ncameras and the new pairs directly reviewed beside their pictures: the hotel's\nown Andreas comparison stays `differs` with the stack station recorded `fixed`\nand the shafts' proportions/heads recorded `open`; the three Carpenter-shop\ncomparisons retain `matches` with the shop anchor byte-identical.\n\nT-2383 remains open and partial.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
